      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Literature data are presented on the possibility of ultrasound diagnosis of coronary artery lesions. Current methods of coronary artery examination are described and echocardiographic criteria of stenosis, atherosclerotic lesions and coronary artery aneurysm are delineated. The authors have examined 10 healthy subjects, 21 patients with coronary heart disease, 1 patient with left main coronary stenosis, 2 patients with proximal stenosis of the right coronary artery, documented by coronaroangiography."},
